<urn:atm:triage:resolution/AY7-QA-002/1>
  a triage:Resolution ;
  triage:resolvedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:resolvedAt "2026-09-07T09:10:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:fixCommit "b4fe93a19" ;
  triage:fixBranch "feature/ay7-windows-herdr-process-installer" ;
  triage:verifiedInRound "qa-pr1285-r3" ;
  triage:resolutionNote "arch-ctm's FIX-AY7-R2 (commits bb657d0ce, b4fe93a19) added if: always() && needs.ci-scope.outputs.runtime == 'true' && matrix.os == 'windows-latest' to the doctor-artifact upload step in .github/workflows/ci.yml (retaining if-no-files-found: error), and filled every row of docs/atm-herdr/windows-process-audit.md's Windows-observation column from real evidence. Verified: gh run view 34098877486 --json jobs shows Test (windows-latest) conclusion=success at head bb657d0ce4324b3526a2ed6f63ec820f26b4a87e, all three Test-matrix legs green; gh api repos/randlee/atm-core/actions/runs/34098877486/artifacts confirms windows-herdr-process-audit-34098877486 present (artifact id 10010390205); downloaded and read windows-ci-doctor.json (herdr.configured=true, breaker.state=closed, 3 CLI-transport endpoints default/blue/green) -- content matches what the doc cites. Read docs/atm-herdr/windows-process-audit.md in full at b4fe93a19: every row cites run 34098877486 and head bb657d0ce4324b3526a2ed6f63ec820f26b4a87e, and rows with evidence gaps honestly state 'not covered' rather than fabricating claims (e.g. live-prompt result, agent-list operation specifics). Cross-checked all 5 test names cited in the doc against the real windows-latest job log (job 101669721560, gh api .../logs --allow-escape-sequences) -- all pass twice with no failures. Secrets/PII sweep of both the doc and the artifact JSON: clean. D5 is satisfied on this evidence." .
